    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19562" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gibbĕrōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		2. gibber, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>badly hump-backed</i> or <i>hunch-backed.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, Auct. ap. <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram.
			9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vel protervi vel gibberosi vel curvi vel
					pruriginosi, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					21, 1, 3</span></i>
			 (al. gibbosi).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sermones,</span>”
				<i>crooked</i>, <i>twisted</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Fronto, Eloqu. p. 231</span></i>
			 Mai. </div>
